  'help.driver-fleet.note5': 'Your earnings screen says who was paid. In a fleet, the money goes to your fleet. In no fleet, it says that what you earned while you drove for one was paid to that fleet, and that nothing is owed to you for it. Money that reached you for work you did on your own is shown beside either.',
  'help.driver-fleet.note6': 'Riding for yourself: when you are in no fleet and ride a bicycle or a motorcycle, Your fleet has “Ride for yourself”. Choose the country you live in — the app then names the company you would ride for — say which vehicle is yours and type its plate. It is done at once: the vehicle is on your start screen, and from then on you are paid directly. Your licence, trips and rating stay as they are. On a van, a truck or anything heavier than a motorcycle it is an ask: add a photograph of your ID card and of your driving licence (and a truck’s body), then “Ask to ride for myself”. Network staff read both and check your record; until they decide nothing changes, and Your fleet says the ask is waiting. You are told on your phone either way — if they say no, with their reason, and you may ask again.',
